; The BlitzLLVM side of the benchmarks: what only BlitzLLVM has. The runners copy it next to the benchmark as bench_compiler.bi
; (bench_original.bi for the original Blitz3D), so that the same program builds with both and their speeds can be compared.

; Which compiler built the program, for the RESULT line.
Function BenchCompiler$()
	Return "llvm"
End Function

; A microsecond timer: microseconds since the start. Only differences are used, so a wrap after 35 minutes does no harm.
Global BenchBase:UInt64 = Microseconds()

Function BenchMicros()
	Return Int(Microseconds() - BenchBase)
End Function

; The draw counters of Stats3D for the last frame.
Function BenchDraws()
	Return Stats3D(1000)
End Function

Function BenchPipelines()
	Return Stats3D(1001)
End Function

Function BenchTextures()
	Return Stats3D(1002)
End Function

Function BenchBuffers()
	Return Stats3D(1003)
End Function

; Shows the frame without waiting for the display (Flip 0), as in the original, so that the time of a frame is the program's and not
; the refresh rate of the display.
Function BenchFlip()
	Flip 0
End Function
